<title>JAPAN: Japan Sept gold imports down 48.6 pct year/year.</title>
<headline>Japan Sept gold imports down 48.6 pct year/year.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's gold imports in September were down 48.6 percent from a year earlier, Finance Ministry data released on Tuesday showed.</p>
<p>	  Figures were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			  Sept 96    Aug 96	Sept 95</p>
<p> Total		   7.86	 9.53	  15.29</p>
<p> Major suppliers:</p>
<p> Australia	     1.82	 1.55	   5.74</p>
<p> South Africa	  0.52	 3.14	   1.05</p>
<p> Britain		 1.63	 1.04	   1.00</p>
<p> Canada		  0.50	 0.21	   0.38</p>
<p> South Korea	   0.70	 1.30	   0.89</p>
<p> Switzerland	   0.01	 0.77	   3.30</p>
<p>Gold imports in the first nine months of 1996 totalled 112.93 tonnes against 214.76 tonnes in the same period last year.</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodities Desk (81-3 3432 7431)</p>
</text>
